message: "If you use the FCP ICSE tool artifact, cite the immutable archived release identified by the paper."
title: "FCP: Capability-Oriented Federation Tool Artifact"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Andersen"
    given-names: "Martin Arthur"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0004-9991-3578"
version: "0.1.0"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Nettking/msh"
url: "https://github.com/Nettking/msh/tree/main/demo/icse"
abstract: >-
  Reviewer artifact for the FCP capability-oriented federation tool demonstration.
  It evaluates selective contribution, capability-specific authority, runtime
  provider eligibility, and durable ownership boundaries using production FCP
  control-plane components with deterministic stand-ins for external physical
  services and observations.
keywords:
  - federation
  - capability-oriented systems
  - digital twins
  - software engineering
  - research software
  - reproducibility
